    <string name="how_title">How it measures</string>
    <string name="how_filters">The raw mic is read at 48 kHz, filtered for A, C and Z weighting, then averaged over 125 ms for Fast or 1 s for Slow. Leq averages the energy, not the decibels, so one loud minute counts for what it was.</string>
    <string name="how_dose">The dose follows NIOSH. 85 dBA for 8 hours is a full day, and every 3 dB louder halves the time.</string>
    <string name="how_over">OVER lights when the input runs out of range, either the converter’s or the mic’s own, which on most phones starts around 120 dB. Anything measured while it is lit reads too low.</string>
    <string name="how_taps">Taps on the screen reach the mic, so the moment around each one is left out of the figures. If another app takes the mic, that stretch is left out too and GAP lights. The alert buzz is counted, since leaving it out would hide the sound that set it off.</string>
    <string name="how_certified">A phone is not a certified meter. For absolute levels, calibrate against one you trust.</string>

